# A `finally` whose only work is a push onto a list of the function's own, which nobody can read once the error has left the function. Selection takes the list out, and the push with it;
# the handler then only throws the error on, so the read in the `catch` block that it covered loses it. The rule that skips such a handler says so, and the check has nothing to report.
# -- source: handler-of-a-dead-finally.js
